{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>All the region of Argob, all that Bashan, is called the land of Rephaim.</b> The meaning: all the region of Argob, all of Bashan, which is called the land of Rephaim — as in the language of \"all that Samuel the seer and Saul son of Kish had dedicated\" (I Chronicles 26:28), \"who had settled foreign women\" (Ezra 10:17), where the ה in them stands in place of אשר, and so there are many instances. And it was called the land of Rephaim either on account of Og, who ruled over it, or because it originally belonged to the Rephaim and was left to Og, for he and the people dwelling in it were from the remnant of the Rephaim."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:36.177894287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}